92186463546} :answer-field/id #uuid "50cc552f-f6da-53d0-8115-14a52ecbc6c5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4af2b663-f664-5687-8b3d-4cb7ed3e89ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463548} {:answer/id #uuid "12a3b8bc-c982-5ad8-998b-0a6fb0036f63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4af2b663-f664-5687-8b3d-4cb7ed3e89ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463548} :answer-field/id #uuid "53b4e1b4-58bf-5e0a-bc9c-2b1223fdcc3c" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464708}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "528091bc-3b41-5908-b5b6-b20261706098" :question/math-academy-id "q-125792" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨1,\\,x⟩$ and the points $A(1,0)$ and $B(e,1)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2(e-1),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2(e-1),$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the segment line $\\overset{―}{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is independent of path.\n\n- **IV.** $F$ is conservative." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Parameterizing the curve, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{1}(t)=⟨t,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in [1,e].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}⟨1,\\,t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,\\frac{1}{t}⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}1+1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}2\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2t\\,{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =2(e-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Parameterizing the line segment, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{2}(t)=⟨t(e-1)+1,\\,t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨1,\\,t(e-1)+1⟩\\cdot ⟨e-1,\\,1⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}e-1+t(e-1)+1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}t(e-1)+e\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{{t}^{2}(e-1)}{2}+et]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{e-1}{2}+e \\\\  & =\\frac{3e-1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ have the same initial and terminal points, yet\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$\n\nwe conclude that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is path-dependent.\n\n- Statement IV is false. If a vector field is conservative then it is path-independent. Since $F$ is path-dependent, it is not conservative."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419017 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172054 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "72015667-33a9-53e2-a0c4-09d8ce916b54" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Fields That Are Independent of Path"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bbc76e1-b401-5a78-abad-35dac56a605e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453342} {:answer/id #uuid "279f518b-43b4-54ff-a27b-f222f36cb0f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "279f518b-43b4-54ff-a27b-f222f36cb0f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453343} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ab559b0-8ad8-5600-af4d-58237670463b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454421} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2848ae05-afe6-565a-9e41-aea348ad8825" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453344} {:answer/id #uuid "b066d196-4087-59b9-80a0-674602ceaaf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b066d196-4087-59b9-80a0-674602ceaaf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453345} :answer-field/id #uuid "029fd954-167e-57fe-8991-0827db39c02c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454422} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa9edb55-47b4-5ffa-8f84-e71046dcce7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453346} {:answer/id #uuid "9b304306-6e7d-5cf9-b636-c3306a1cc7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa9edb55-47b4-5ffa-8f84-e71046dcce7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453346} :answer-field/id #uuid "1eb5c926-ae08-5e20-a8c6-c74a02337973" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454423} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2382595d-1329-5487-addb-48a96fc302ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453348} {:answer/id #uuid "ccaebe90-5c00-5752-8300-47cb5c96cc81" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2382595d-1329-5487-addb-48a96fc302ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453348} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0ae2286-b965-58b3-9eee-07c2cde691c4" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b47df0de-b5ee-5562-b36a-a659cbe48d85" :question/math-academy-id "q-125796" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F(x,y)=⟨-y,\\,x⟩$ and the points $A(0,1)$ and $B(0,-1)$ in the $xy$-plane. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne 0,$ where ${C}_{1}$ is the path along the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=1,$ traversed from $A$ to $B$ in counterclockwise direction.\n\n- **II.** ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is the path along the segment line $\\overset{―}{AB},$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$\n\n- **III.** ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is independent of path.\n\n- **IV.** $F$ is conservative." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be a piecewise-smooth curve given by the vector-valued function $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b].$ Let $f$ be a differentiable function of two or three variables such that $∇f$ is continuous on $C.$ The fundamental theorem for line integrals states that \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}∇f\\cdot \\text{d}r=f(r(b))-f(r(a)).\n$$\n\n \n\nThis theorem implies that the line integral of a conservative vector field depends only on the value of $f$ at the initial and terminal points $A$ and $B,$ and is independent of the path between them.\n\nWith that in mind, we consider each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Parameterizing the curve, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{1}(t)=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,\\,t\\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{3\\pi }{2}].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\cdot ⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2}1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =t{|}_{\\pi /2}^{3\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\pi  \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Parameterizing the line segment, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{2}(t)=⟨0,\\,1-2t⟩,\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}⟨2t-1,\\,0⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\,-2⟩\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}0\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ have the same initial and terminal points, yet\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r\\ne {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$\n\nwe conclude that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ is path-dependent.\n\n- Statement IV is false. If a vector field is conservative then it is path-independent. Since $F$ is path-dependent, it is not conservative."}]}
